  "conclusions": [
    "Main already misses the median performance/LCP target without IBM Plex; round 1 typography is not the sole cause.",
    "Both LCP elements are the unchanged eager, high-priority, preloaded hero images, not text or font elements.",
    "Sans-preload-only repeats show no material gain: median home 3338ms versus real round 1 3369ms; service 3331ms versus 3333ms. Keep the original source preload.",
    "Blocking all JS requests yields home 98 / 2339ms and service 99 / 2258ms, relative to proxy control home 92 / 3360ms and service 92 / 3353ms. The 1021/1095ms difference bounds modeled initial JS/network cost; this is not a behavior-preserving fix or an accepted production floor.",
    "Critical-only inline CSS improves FCP but worsens LCP. A second probe holds full CSS until 2.24s; initial hero presentation still follows framework evaluation, so the proposed scheduling mechanism does not help.",
    "No large avoidable app callback was found before LCP. Core Next/React modules dominate; the full quote-form import occurs after observed LCP and chat code loads on first open.",
    "Localhost reports contain no third-party analytics requests because of production-host gating; they cannot measure production third-party transfer cost.",
    "The remaining gap is measured for the tested build/settings, not a mathematical proof that 98 is impossible under every future architecture."
  ],
